  "body": "### Summary\n\nCheck whether the legacy-app bug \"Topic-list pager: a link without `href` must not break the parser\" exists in SwiftHFR (test on the lots named below) and fix it if so. Found by Bybifok (@moust4ki) in the legacy app.\n\n### Scope\n\nSwiftHFR work (from `docs/LOTS.md` \"Issues to open\" #1): Non-regression test in LOT-022 (#50) (and LOT-021 (#49), later 024/MP lists): skip the entry, keep the rows\n\nLegacy commit: `237db70` (see [ezzz/HFRnow#3](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/3)).\n\nStatus in LOTS.md: todo.\n\n### Related lots\n\nLOT-021 (#49), LOT-022 (#50)\n\n### Depends on\n\n—\n\n### Credit\n\nFound by Bybifok (@moust4ki); credit the finding in the fix (label `moust4ki aka bybifok finding`). Legacy fix: ezzz/HFRnow#3 (open).\n\n### PRs\n\n- [ezzz/HFRnow#3](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/3) — Bybifok's legacy-app corrections (open, not ours)\n- [ezzz/HFRnow#13](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/pull/13) — backlog of the findings in LOTS.md (merged)\n\n### Help wanted\n\n@moust4ki, you found this one: would you like to take it? The work is to check whether the bug exists in SwiftHFR (a test on the lots above) and, if it does, to fix it, with the credit to you. The code exists: the list parsers are merged (LOT-021 (#49), LOT-022 (#50); LOT-024 (#52) already added a test for a last-page link without `href`). Verification can start now.\n\nTo take it, comment `/claim <your session id>` (e.g. `/claim human/moust4ki`) and open a PR into `dev-swift` with `Closes #<this issue>` (AGENTS.md §8, CONTRIBUTING.md). If you would rather not, say so and a maintainer session will pick it up.\n",
